cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
type: software
title: Life of a Photon
abstract: A first-person, physically based visualisation of what an observer with mass sees while travelling along a night-time city avenue at any constant speed from rest to 0.99999 c, with relativistic aberration, Doppler shift and the transformation of radiance computed spectrally in real time, accompanied by a bilingual (Turkish and English) scientific dossier inside the application.
authors:
  - name: cayankuzu
repository-code: https://github.com/cayankuzu/LifeOfPhoton
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-11
keywords:
  - special relativity
  - relativistic aberration
  - Doppler effect
  - Terrell rotation
  - Lorentz contraction
  - transformation of radiance
  - colorimetry
  - real-time rendering
  - WebGL
